  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thai Nguyen Redcross</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam and Red Cross&#x2019; response in Thai Nguyen will be implemented in partnership with the provincial Red Cross (local implementing partner), the other key stakeholders such as, Department of Agriculture and Environment (DAE), the Women&#x2019;s Union and the Hanoi Association of Persons with Disabilities (OPD). Oxfam will coordinate activities, ensure technical support, procurement, reporting, and compliance. This partnership model reflects Oxfam&#x2019;s global commitment to localisation, working through existing relationships with thePeople&#x2019;s Aid Coordinating Committee (PACCOM), the Vietnam Dykes and Disaster Management Authority (VDDMA), and the provincial Red Cross. This six-month humanitarian project will be focusing on:
&#x2022; Emergency Food Security &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Livelihoods (EFSL):
o Multi-PurposeCash Assistance (MPCA) for immediate needs
o Cash for nutrition for pregnant/lactating women, PLwDs, and female frontline workers
oConditional Cash-for-Work (CfW) to repair key community and agricultural infrastructure
&#x2022; Water,Sanitation &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Hygiene (WASH):
o Distribution of water containers and dignity kits for women and girls
o Hygiene promotion and school-based awareness activities
o Water quality testing and CfW for WASH infrastructure restoration
Oxfam will also providetraining on safeguarding, gender, and protection, establish feedback mechanisms and relief committees ensuring gender, ethnic, and disability inclusion, and pilot a Cash-for-Care Work (CfCW) scheme for women first responders.
Building on existing partnerships in Thai Nguyen from the DFAT-funded WEAVE project and ongoing women-led livelihood programs and local expertise, as well as Oxfam&#x2019;s extensive experience in humanitarian responses,including the Central Flooding Emergency in four provinces (2020&#x2013;2021), COVID-19 emergency relief and recovery efforts (2022&#x2013;2024),and more recent responses to Typhoons Yagi and Wipha in Northern Vietnam in 2024 and 2025, Oxfam&#x2019;s integrated and culturally sensitive response will address urgent humanitarian needs while strengthening local resilience and disaster preparedness in the province.</narrative>
  </description>
